Laptop profile — optional role-based desktop
application launcher. It does not alter power-management services automatically.

If using FVWM, you may also copy the workstation profile's FVWM function and add
  + I Function DesktopProfileStartup
inside your existing StartFunction. The laptop profile itself does not overwrite
any existing FVWM configuration.

Clock: edit boot-mode next to mcfg to "standalone" (Linux only, RTC in UTC) or "dual-boot"
(Linux + Windows, RTC in local time), then run `sudo ./mcfg apply laptop`.
scripts/hwclock.apply writes the hardware clock; it is not rolled back by `mcfg rollback`.
